%N A397825 Number of equivalence classes of partitions of n, where two partitions are equivalent if and only if their multisets of part multiplicities are isomorphic.
%C A397825 Two multisets are isomorphic if there is a bijection between their underlying sets that preserves multiplicities. For example, {1,1,2} and {2,2,3} are isomorphic.
%C A397825 The same count is obtained for compositions instead of partitions.
%H A397825 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A397825/b397825.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%F A397825 For a nonempty partition lambda = (lambda_1,...,lambda_k), with lambda_1 >= ... >= lambda_k, let s_i = Sum_{j=i..k} lambda_j and M(lambda) = Sum_{i=1..k} binomial(s_i+1,2).
%F A397825 For n >= 1, a(n) is the number of nonempty partitions lambda with M(lambda) <= n. Also a(0) = 1.
%e A397825 For n = 4, the partitions (4), (3,1), (2,2), (2,1,1), and (1,1,1,1) have multisets of part multiplicities {1}, {1,1}, {2}, {1,2}, and {4}, respectively.
%e A397825 The three isomorphism classes are {{1},{2},{4}}, {{1,1}}, and {{1,2}}, so a(4) = 3.
%Y A397825 Cf. A088887, A056556.
%K A397825 nonn,new
